{"ts": "2026-11-09T21:26:25.240706Z", "run_id": "r-20261109T2122Z-5daf", "unit": "openspec:add-tool-registry", "seq": 12, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-007", "id": "Q-007", "status": "answered", "reason": "Every THEN clause of the scenario is asserted by the tracing test, and the code paths behind each assertion (two-step approval, lock-first second transaction, recheck, conflict mapping, imported_by from the actor) are present as design.md describes.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "C-6d84e4c8", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-007+5", "batch_size": 5, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.633075, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "f76a74bda66d82bf45d21400b582451b72e31f8fe46584c22d1147ffc300ee85", "checked": [{"ref": "src/tools/approve.test.ts:411", "quote": "assert.equal(afterAcme.length, 22);", "claim": "The test asserts 22 block rows after acme is approved."}, {"ref": "src/tools/approve.test.ts:414", "quote": "ref: \"acme.lookup_vendor@1\",\n        binding: { server: \"acme\", tool: \"lookup_vendor\" },\n        content_hash: H_LV_F,\n        imported_by: \"u_dave\",", "claim": "The test asserts the binding, hash and importer of acme.lookup_vendor@1."}, {"ref": "src/tools/approve.test.ts:437", "quote": "const failing = rejectingPool(db.appPool, (text) =>\n      /UPDATE ursitoare\\.tool_surface/.test(text),", "claim": "The failed second step is injected on the tool_surface UPDATE as the scenario says."}, {"ref": "src/tools/approve.test.ts:480", "quote": "assert.equal(gammaImports.length, 1);", "claim": "The repeat writes no second registry.block_imported event for gamma's ref."}, {"ref": "src/tools/approve.test.ts:511", "quote": "refusal(\"ref_conflict\"),", "claim": "The delta race is asserted to reject with ref_conflict."}, {"ref": "src/tools/approve.test.ts:546", "quote": "refusal(\"digest_mismatch\"),", "claim": "The zeta race is asserted to reject with digest_mismatch."}, {"ref": "src/tools/approve.test.ts:555", "quote": "assert.equal(zetaBlocks.length, 25);", "claim": "The test asserts 25 block rows at the end."}, {"ref": "src/tools/store.ts:466", "quote": "const locked = await tx.query<ServerRow>(\n      `SELECT ${SERVER_COLUMNS} FROM ursitoare.tool_server\n       WHERE tenant_id = $1 AND tool_server_id = $2 FOR UPDATE`,", "claim": "The second transaction locks the server row as its first statement."}, {"ref": "src/tools/store.ts:476", "quote": "if (newest === null || newest.approved_by !== null || newest.surface_digest !== input.digest) {\n      throw refused(\"digest_mismatch\");", "claim": "The second transaction rechecks the newest surface before writing."}, {"ref": "src/tools/store.ts:456", "quote": "if (error instanceof RegistryError && error.code === \"REGISTRY_CONFLICT\") {\n      throw refused(\"ref_conflict\");", "claim": "A registry conflict becomes TOOLS_REFUSED ref_conflict."}, {"ref": "src/registry/block-store.ts:122", "quote": "if (hash !== undefined && hash !== block.contentHash) {\n          throw new RegistryError(\"REGISTRY_CONFLICT\"", "claim": "importCatalogue conflicts only on a different hash and otherwise reports the ref unchanged."}, {"ref": "src/tools/directory.test.ts:326", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(await directory.resolve(solo, \"gamma.lookup_vendor@1\"), BIND_GAMMA);", "claim": "The directory test asserts gamma's resolve result after the repeat."}]}
